From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:03:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] Round 8: Decode parameter arrays with an exact fast
 path

Decode candidate batches first with a twin of Candidate whose
parameters are borrowed as a raw JSON slice and parsed in one pass
under the strict JSON number grammar. Numbers with at most 19 digits,
a mantissa up to 2^53 and a decimal exponent within 22 use one exact
multiply or divide (Clinger's fast path); other numbers use str::parse.
Both round correctly, as serde_json's float_roundtrip parser does, so
values are identical. Any fast-path failure re-decodes the document
with the reference types, keeping results and error messages exactly
as before. The CLI request path uses the same scheme. Unit tests
compare both decoders on edge cases and on 20,000 random samples in
several notations, and check an identical CLI error.

Workload: invalid (1,024 full records with 63 parameters each, one
worker).
Before median: 1.615 ms. After median: 1.198 ms. Speedup: 1.35x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
